<title>BRAZIL: Brazil gov't staff reductions fail to meet target.</title>
<headline>Brazil gov't staff reductions fail to meet target.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>A voluntary staff reduction program, aimed at reducing payroll spending by Brazil's federal government, attracted about one third of the government's original target, a goverment spokesman said.</p>
<p>A total of 10,865 federal workers had agreed to leave their jobs compared with a target of 32,000, a spokesman for the Administration Ministry said.</p>
